From: apex project <apex@kernel>
Subject: [PATCH] bbg: add CONFIG_BBG_BLOCK_RECOVERY for efisp exploit allowlist

Adds a new Kconfig option to control recovery partition protection
in the default allowlist. The efisp-exploit allowlist always includes
recovery regardless of this setting.

Source: https://github.com/WildKernels/kernel_patches/tree/main/common/bbg

Signed-off-by: apex project

--- a/Baseband-guard/Kconfig	2026-08-29 16:51:24.525700154 +0200
+++ b/Baseband-guard/Kconfig	2026-08-29 16:51:24.585459734 +0200
@@ -35,6 +35,16 @@
           fastboot mode).
           If unsure, leave this n.
 
+config BBG_BLOCK_RECOVERY
+       bool "Enable Baseband Protection for Recovery Partition"
+       depends on BBG
+       default n
+       help
+         Enable protection for recovery partition in the default
+         (secure) allowlist. The efisp-exploit allowlist always
+         includes recovery regardless of this setting.
+         If unsure, leave this n.
+
 config BBG_DOMAIN_PROTECTION
        bool "Interception for malicious Selinux domain switching"
        depends on BBG
